  "summary": "I wrote the breakout game in `src/main.ts`. It typechecks, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser here, so the rendering and gameplay are untested.\n\n- **Scene:** It uses the `neon-arcade` look with a perspective camera facing the field. There are 8 columns by 5 rows of bricks, each row a different color and worth 50, 40, 30, 20 and 10 points from the top.\n- **Controls and rules:** Left/Right or A/D move the paddle, Space serves, and R restarts at any time. The paddle bounce angle depends on where the ball lands. Lives start at 3, and losing the last one sets `lost`. Clearing every brick sets `won`.\n- **HUD and state:** A DOM HUD below the canvas shows score, lives and status. A full-canvas overlay with a restart hint appears on win or loss. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is a getter returning `{ status, score, lives, bricksLeft }`.\n- **Loop:** The game runs on its own `requestAnimationFrame` loop and moves the scene nodes each frame. `window.__TASK_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and the first drawn frame.\n- **Limitation:** If `app.ready()` never resolves or rejects, `__TASK_READY__` is never set.\n\n",
